.TH HYDD.CONF 5 "2026-11-22" "hydd 0.4.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
hydd.conf \- configuration for the hydd Hydrus PTR mirror daemon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hydd.conf
is a plain-text
.I key = value
file. Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
or
.B ;
are ignored. Values may optionally be quoted with single or double quotes.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B data_dir
Directory for the store, delta journal, state, and generated keys. Default
.IR /var/lib/hyd .
.TP
.B compression
Select the storage backend.
.I true
(the default) uses the compact custom columnar store, roughly 25-30 GB for a
full mirror.
.I false
uses a plain SQLite database at
.IR <data_dir>/sqlite/hyd.sqlite3 ,
roughly 45-60 GB and easier to inspect.
Changing the value after a store exists is refused; use a fresh data
directory. This is a mirror schema, not the multi-file Hydrus client schema.
.TP
.B listen_address ", " listen_port
API bind address and port. Defaults
.I 127.0.0.1
and
.IR 45869 .
.TP
.B access_key ", " access_key_file
API access key. If left empty, the key is read from
.I access_key_file
or generated there on first start.
.TP
.B require_localhost_key
By default, loopback TCP peers (127.0.0.1, ::1) skip the API key check, and
bogus keys are ignored too. Set this to true to require a valid access key
from localhost as well. The check uses the socket peer, not X-Forwarded-For.
Default false. If a public reverse proxy connects from loopback, loopback trust
makes the read-only API public through that proxy.
.TP
.B service_key ", " service_key_file
Service key reported by the API. Generated if empty.
.TP
.B service_name
Human-readable tag service name. Default
.IR "public tag repository" .
.TP
.B repository_url ", " repository_access_key
Upstream Hydrus repository. The defaults are the real PTR and its shared
read-only key.
.TP
.B sync_enabled
Enable or disable all repository syncing. Default true.
.TP
.B sync_on_start
Sync immediately at startup instead of waiting one interval. Default true.
.TP
.B sync_interval_seconds
Seconds between metadata checks. Minimum 60. Default 3600.
.TP
.B partitions
Number of custom-store partitions. Must be a power of two between 1 and 64.
Default 16.
.TP
.B compaction_enabled
For the custom store, merge the append-only delta journal into the base store
when it grows past
\fIcompact_after_delta_mb\fR. Default true. Compaction never deletes live tags
or mappings; disabling it keeps the raw delta journal intact and increases
startup memory over time.
.TP
.B compact_after_delta_mb
Delta size that triggers automatic compaction. Zero disables the threshold.
Default 512.
.TP
.B keep_update_cache
Keep downloaded update files after a successful initial build. Default false.
.TP
.B download_workers
Number of parallel update-file downloads. Each worker reuses one TLS
connection. Default 8; maximum 32.
.TP
.B download_timeout_seconds
Per-request timeout. Default 120.
.TP
.B download_rate_limit_kib
Optional download rate limit in KiB/s. Zero means unlimited.
.TP
.B log_file
Rotating log file. Empty disables file logging. Default
.IR /var/log/hyd/hyd.log .
.TP
.B log_rotate_mb
Rotate the plaintext log at this size. Default 10.
.TP
.B log_rotate_keep
Number of old compressed logs to retain. Default 5.
.TP
.B log_rotate_compress
Gzip old logs. Default true.
.TP
.B log_level
One of trace, debug, info, warn, error, off. Default info.
.TP
.B max_download_bytes ", " max_update_index
Test/development limits. A partial store is produced when
.B max_update_index
is set. Automated tests against the real PTR must stay under 10 GiB.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/hydd.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hydd (8)
